    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1ed3bb67-51a8-5170-873d-959b19dff123",
      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $3-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{7}}}$ for $y>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(3-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{7}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y &= \\int \\left(3-\\frac{1}{y^{\\frac{7}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= 3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}y-\\int y^{-\\frac{7}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= 3\\frac{y^{0+1}}{(0+1)}-\\frac{y^{-\\frac{7}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{7}{2}+1)}+C \\\\ &= 3y+\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{y^{5}}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
