      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(t^{5}-6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(t^{5}-6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(t^{5}-6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int t^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-6\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\frac{t^{5+1}}{(5+1)}-6\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= \\frac{t^{6}}{6}-6t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
